h is 610.5. Then I'll divide the difference (165) by 610.5 and multiply by 100. This gives me approximately 27.0% when rounded to the nearest tenth.\n\nI'll round the result to 27.0% to match the required precision of one decimal place.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_769997c0de92473aa2a9995e","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"todo__todo_write","arguments":{"content":"- [x] Find total federal expenditures for February 1938\n- [x] Find total federal expenditures for January 1939\n- [ ] Calculate absolute percent difference\n- [ ] Round to nearest tenths place\n- [ ] Write answer to /app/answer.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"todo"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
